WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.332
Views matter because they let us define important logic once and reuse it.

00:00:05.332 --> 00:00:10.367
Suppose five reports all need the same patient and admission join.

00:00:10.367 --> 00:00:14.017
We could copy that join into five different queries.

00:00:14.017 --> 00:00:19.072
But if the logic changes later, we now have five places to update.

00:00:19.072 --> 00:00:24.037
A view gives that shared logic one name and one definition.

00:00:24.037 --> 00:00:28.962
Reports can query the view instead of rebuilding the same steps.

00:00:28.962 --> 00:00:34.192
A view can also expose only the columns that are useful for a task.

00:00:34.192 --> 00:00:40.511
That can reduce accidental exposure, but permissions still need to be configured separately.
